Automatic Rollback on Validation Failure

A production-grade CI/CD pipeline should automatically revert to the last known good endpoint configuration when validation fails.

Rollback Strategy
Deploy New Model
        │
        ▼
Create New EndpointConfig
        │
        ▼
Update Endpoint
        │
        ▼
Run Validation Suite
        │
 ┌──────┴──────┐
 │             │
PASS         FAIL
 │             │
 ▼             ▼
Promote    Rollback
                │
                ▼
Restore Previous EndpointConfig



Step 1: Capture Current Endpoint Configuration

Before deployment, save the active configuration.

CURRENT_CONFIG=$(aws sagemaker describe-endpoint \
  --endpoint-name my-endpoint \
  --query EndpointConfigName \
  --output text)

echo "$CURRENT_CONFIG" > previous_config.txt

Example:
my-endpoint-config-v12

Step 2: Deploy New Configuration
aws sagemaker update-endpoint \
    --endpoint-name my-endpoint \
    --endpoint-config-name my-endpoint-config-v13


Step 3: Automated Rollback Function
rollback_endpoint.sh
#!/bin/bash

ENDPOINT_NAME="$1"
ROLLBACK_CONFIG="$2"

echo "================================="
echo "ROLLBACK INITIATED"
echo "================================="

echo "Endpoint: $ENDPOINT_NAME"
echo "Rollback Config: $ROLLBACK_CONFIG"

aws sagemaker update-endpoint \
    --endpoint-name "$ENDPOINT_NAME" \
    --endpoint-config-name "$ROLLBACK_CONFIG"

echo "Waiting for rollback..."

while true
do
    STATUS=$(aws sagemaker describe-endpoint \
        --endpoint-name "$ENDPOINT_NAME" \
        --query EndpointStatus \
        --output text)

    echo "Status: $STATUS"

    if [ "$STATUS" = "InService" ]; then
        echo "Rollback completed."
        exit 0
    fi

    if [ "$STATUS" = "Failed" ]; then
        echo "Rollback failed."
        exit 1
    fi

    sleep 30
done


Step 4: Integrate Rollback Into Validation Pipeline

Update validation script:
ROLLBACK_CONFIG=$(cat previous_config.txt)

rollback() {

    echo "Validation failed."

    ./rollback_endpoint.sh \
       "$ENDPOINT_NAME" \
       "$ROLLBACK_CONFIG"

    exit 1
}

Example Validation Gate
Instead of:
if [ "$AVG" -gt "$MAX_AVG_LATENCY_MS" ]; then
    exit 1
fi

Use:
if [ "$AVG" -gt "$MAX_AVG_LATENCY_MS" ]; then
    echo "Latency SLA violated."
    rollback
fi

